From: OpenWrt <noreply@openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] netfilter: bridge: Add conntrack support for VLAN
 and PPPoE encapsulation

Extend bridge conntrack to handle packets carrying a single outer
VLAN tag or PPPoE encapsulation, optionally with one inner VLAN tag
inside the PPPoE frame.

Add nf_ct_bridge_inner() to parse PPPoE and inner VLAN headers from
the skb. The function returns the byte offset to pull past these
headers so callers can reach the inner IP/IPv6 payload.

Key changes:

- Use sizeof(struct pppoe_hdr) = 6 to locate the PPP protocol id
  (PPPOE_SES_HLEN = 8 includes the proto bytes; the proto itself
  sits at phdr + 6).

- Use struct vlan_hdr (4 bytes) for inner VLAN inside PPPoE frames,
  not struct vlan_ethhdr (18 bytes) which would read past the skb
  when the inner tag has no embedded MAC addresses.

- After __skb_pull(skb, offset) in the IP/IPv6 cases of
  nf_ct_bridge_pre and nf_ct_bridge_refrag, call
  skb_reset_network_header(skb) so network_header tracks the inner
  IP header for ip_hdr/ipv6_hdr/skb_ip_totlen.

- Restore L2 headers on error paths via a do_not_track_push label
  before marking the packet untracked.

- Balance __skb_pull with __skb_push on the success path of
  nf_ct_bridge_pre before calling nf_conntrack_in().

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Build <build@openwrt.org>
---
